{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ECVvYJWXawzNZNgzFdVrjG","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# Pixel Engine API (v0.46.0)\n5:## Sections\n23:## 1. Engine and games\n25:### ADAPTIVE_ASPECT\n33:### type AspectMode\n39:### BUILTIN_MODELS\n47:### chunkyResolution()\n55:### clearScene()\n63:### computeFraming()\n69:### countObjects()\n77:### type DebugAction\n87:### type DebugKeyChanges\n95:### type DebugKeyMap\n101:### type DebugKeysOption\n114:### DEFAULT_DEBUG_KEYS\n122:### disposeObject()\n132:### class Engine\n197:### ENGINE_VERSION\n203:### interface EngineOptions\n226:### FPS_OPTIONS\n232:### class FrameLimiter\n242:### frameView()\n253:### interface Framing\n266:### interface Game\n288:### interface GameContext\n305:### interface HeadlessOptions\n312:### class LoadingScreen\n323:### loadSettings()\n331:### normalizeSettings()\n339:### optionsFromUrl()\n352:### PIXEL_SIZES\n358:### interface PlayerSettings\n372:### QUALITY\n381:### QUALITY_LEVELS\n387:### QUALITY_OPTIONS\n393:### type QualityLevel\n407:### type QualityOption\n413:### interface QualitySettings\n418:### rebindDebugKeys()\n428:### interface Resolution\n446:### RESOLUTIONS\n452:### resolveDebugKeys()\n460:### class Settings\n479:### interface SettingsHost\n492:### class SettingsPanel\n507:### storeSettings()\n513:### urlSettings()\n523:### interface Viewport\n531:### withUrlOptions()\n542:## 2. Camera\n544:### CAMERA_PRESETS\n550:### interface CameraConfig\n566:### type CameraPreset\n577:### class CameraRig\n604:### interface CameraRigState\n617:### createCameraRig()\n623:### class FirstPersonRig\n637:### class FreeRig\n655:### class OrthoRig\n666:### class ThirdPersonRig\n677:## 3. Rendering, looks and filters\n679:### AMOUNT\n687:### applyFilter()\n696:### applyFilters()\n704:### type BackendName\n712:### interface CapturedFrame\n718:### clampParam()\n726:### cloneLook()\n732:### DEFAULT_EDGES\n738:### DEFAULT_PIXEL\n744:### defaultLook()\n752:### defaultParams()\n760:### interface EdgeSettings\n765:### FILTER_IDS\n771:### FILTER_PRESETS\n779:### interface FilterContext\n786:### interface FilterDef\n798:### type FilterGroup\n804:### filterOrder()\n812:### interface FilterParam\n# Pixel Engine 0.46.0\n\nA WebGPU engine that renders 3D scenes as authentic pixel art (WebGPU only), with\nRapier physics, a platformer character with a full animation set, pixel HUD, audio, particles\nand a look system (filters per layer). This folder is everything a game needs.\n\nRead in this order:\n\n1. `GUIDE.md` (~15k tokens): how to host a game, the mental model, a complete game, recipes, the rules and common mistakes. Read it whole.\n2. `API.md` (~62k tokens): every export with its signature and doc. Search it; don't read it whole.\n3. `game.js`: the guide's quick start, a complete game. Edit it into yours.\n4. `ASSETS.md` (~4k tokens), when the game builds with models and textures: the library, the format, the loop and the style rules. Read it whole; `LIBRARY.md` (~44k tokens) lists every model and texture, built in or from a pack: search it (or filter `library.json`).\n\n| File | What |\n| --- | --- |\n| `pixel-engine.js` | The engine, 4750 KB: one ES module with three.js (`THREE`, `TSL`), Rapier and its wasm, the hero kit, the built-in models (`assets/coin.glb`, `assets/hero.glb`, `assets/tree.glb`) and the engine CSS. Never edit it. |\n| `index.html`, `game.js` | A game to start from: serve this folder over HTTP and open `index.html` |\n| `examples/` | The guides' other recipes as pages (`side-scroller`, `top-down`, `looks`, `market`) and the modules they import (`market-models.js`) |\n| `check.mjs` | `node check.mjs [page] [--keys KeyD*60,Space*4] [--cameras] [--looks a,b]`: plays the page in a real browser, saves screenshots, fails on any error. Run it before you hand a game back. `node check.mjs --headless game.js` plays the game in Node with no browser and replays it (GUIDE.md section 8); `node check.mjs --sheets models.js` draws your models and textures (ASSETS.md) |\n| `ASSETS.md`, `LIBRARY.md`, `CREDITS.md` | Models and textures as data; the built-in library and the imported packs, by family; where everything the kit carries came from (ship it with your game) |\n| `library.json` | Every model and texture as data (id, kind, family, pack, tags, size, licence): filter it to find what a game needs |\n| `packs/` | Imported packs (`packs/index.json` lists them): `loadPack('packs/<id>.json')` |\n| `pixel-engine.d.ts`, `types/` | TypeScript declarations (optional) |\n| `CHANGELOG.md` | What changed between engine versions |\n| `LICENSE` | The engine's licence (MIT) |\n| `manifest.json` | Version, build, where newer versions are (`latest`, `releases`, `source`) and every file with its size |\n\nServe it: `npx serve .` or `python3 -m http.server` here, then open http://localhost:3000/ (or :8000).\nES modules don't load from `file://`.\n\nNewer versions: the newest release of the kit is always https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip, and every release stays\nat https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases with what changed in it. To build one from\nthe engine's repository instead: `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight && cd riftlight && npm ci && npm run bundle`\nmakes `bundle/pixel-engine/`. To upgrade a game, see GUIDE.md, section 10.\nlooks.html\nlooks.js\nmarket-models.js\nmarket.html\nmarket.js\nside-scroller.html\nside-scroller.js\ntop-down.html\ntop-down.js","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f147b5a-afdb-41c5-bbfc-62264f8c7cee","uuid":"80e09f9d-9049-4f9f-aac9-0ee8b796799d","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:21:07.580Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1:# Pixel Engine API (v0.46.0)\n5:## Sections\n23:## 1. Engine and games\n25:### ADAPTIVE_ASPECT\n33:### type AspectMode\n39:### BUILTIN_MODELS\n47:### chunkyResolution()\n55:### clearScene()\n63:### computeFraming()\n69:### countObjects()\n77:### type DebugAction\n87:### type DebugKeyChanges\n95:### type DebugKeyMap\n101:### type DebugKeysOption\n114:### DEFAULT_DEBUG_KEYS\n122:### disposeObject()\n132:### class Engine\n197:### ENGINE_VERSION\n203:### interface EngineOptions\n226:### FPS_OPTIONS\n232:### class FrameLimiter\n242:### frameView()\n253:### interface Framing\n266:### interface Game\n288:### interface GameContext\n305:### interface HeadlessOptions\n312:### class LoadingScreen\n323:### loadSettings()\n331:### normalizeSettings()\n339:### optionsFromUrl()\n352:### PIXEL_SIZES\n358:### interface PlayerSettings\n372:### QUALITY\n381:### QUALITY_LEVELS\n387:### QUALITY_OPTIONS\n393:### type QualityLevel\n407:### type QualityOption\n413:### interface QualitySettings\n418:### rebindDebugKeys()\n428:### interface Resolution\n446:### RESOLUTIONS\n452:### resolveDebugKeys()\n460:### class Settings\n479:### interface SettingsHost\n492:### class SettingsPanel\n507:### storeSettings()\n513:### urlSettings()\n523:### interface Viewport\n531:### withUrlOptions()\n542:## 2. Camera\n544:### CAMERA_PRESETS\n550:### interface CameraConfig\n566:### type CameraPreset\n577:### class CameraRig\n604:### interface CameraRigState\n617:### createCameraRig()\n623:### class FirstPersonRig\n637:### class FreeRig\n655:### class OrthoRig\n666:### class ThirdPersonRig\n677:## 3. Rendering, looks and filters\n679:### AMOUNT\n687:### applyFilter()\n696:### applyFilters()\n704:### type BackendName\n712:### interface CapturedFrame\n718:### clampParam()\n726:### cloneLook()\n732:### DEFAULT_EDGES\n738:### DEFAULT_PIXEL\n744:### defaultLook()\n752:### defaultParams()\n760:### interface EdgeSettings\n765:### FILTER_IDS\n771:### FILTER_PRESETS\n779:### interface FilterContext\n786:### interface FilterDef\n798:### type FilterGroup\n804:### filterOrder()\n812:### interface FilterParam\n# Pixel Engine 0.46.0\n\nA WebGPU engine that renders 3D scenes as authentic pixel art (WebGPU only), with\nRapier physics, a platformer character with a full animation set, pixel HUD, audio, particles\nand a look system (filters per layer). This folder is everything a game needs.\n\nRead in this order:\n\n1. `GUIDE.md` (~15k tokens): how to host a game, the mental model, a complete game, recipes, the rules and common mistakes. Read it whole.\n2. `API.md` (~62k tokens): every export with its signature and doc. Search it; don't read it whole.\n3. `game.js`: the guide's quick start, a complete game. Edit it into yours.\n4. `ASSETS.md` (~4k tokens), when the game builds with models and textures: the library, the format, the loop and the style rules. Read it whole; `LIBRARY.md` (~44k tokens) lists every model and texture, built in or from a pack: search it (or filter `library.json`).\n\n| File | What |\n| --- | --- |\n| `pixel-engine.js` | The engine, 4750 KB: one ES module with three.js (`THREE`, `TSL`), Rapier and its wasm, the hero kit, the built-in models (`assets/coin.glb`, `assets/hero.glb`, `assets/tree.glb`) and the engine CSS. Never edit it. |\n| `index.html`, `game.js` | A game to start from: serve this folder over HTTP and open `index.html` |\n| `examples/` | The guides' other recipes as pages (`side-scroller`, `top-down`, `looks`, `market`) and the modules they import (`market-models.js`) |\n| `check.mjs` | `node check.mjs [page] [--keys KeyD*60,Space*4] [--cameras] [--looks a,b]`: plays the page in a real browser, saves screenshots, fails on any error. Run it before you hand a game back. `node check.mjs --headless game.js` plays the game in Node with no browser and replays it (GUIDE.md section 8); `node check.mjs --sheets models.js` draws your models and textures (ASSETS.md) |\n| `ASSETS.md`, `LIBRARY.md`, `CREDITS.md` | Models and textures as data; the built-in library and the imported packs, by family; where everything the kit carries came from (ship it with your game) |\n| `library.json` | Every model and texture as data (id, kind, family, pack, tags, size, licence): filter it to find what a game needs |\n| `packs/` | Imported packs (`packs/index.json` lists them): `loadPack('packs/<id>.json')` |\n| `pixel-engine.d.ts`, `types/` | TypeScript declarations (optional) |\n| `CHANGELOG.md` | What changed between engine versions |\n| `LICENSE` | The engine's licence (MIT) |\n| `manifest.json` | Version, build, where newer versions are (`latest`, `releases`, `source`) and every file with its size |\n\nServe it: `npx serve .` or `python3 -m http.server` here, then open http://localhost:3000/ (or :8000).\nES modules don't load from `file://`.\n\nNewer versions: the newest release of the kit is always https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip, and every release stays\nat https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases with what changed in it. To build one from\nthe engine's repository instead: `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight && cd riftlight && npm ci && npm run bundle`\nmakes `bundle/pixel-engine/`. To upgrade a game, see GUIDE.md, section 10.\nlooks.html\nlooks.js\nmarket-models.js\nmarket.html\nmarket.js\nside-scroller.html\nside-scroller.js\ntop-down.html\ntop-down.js","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01ECVvYJWXawzNZNgzFdVrjG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
