{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Read, TaskStop, ToolSearch</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user ran `/goal`: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\" STAGE.md: build the game PLAN.md describes; take file names and hand-ins from TASK.md; keep progress in PROGRESS.md. TASK.md: an original game inspired by Animal Crossing: City Folk, on the riftlight engine kit (engine unmodified), single HTML `[GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-171821].html`, dev subfolder of the same name, code-only audio, music 10% default, gibberish voices, AI Hub multiplayer plus on its own, dev mode from pause with live sliders and reset, attract at 10 s idle, controller-first 10-foot UI, touch-only notice, no TODOs/stubs, `exit-interview.json` in exact shape, Source Information + Testing/Engine/Prompt Feedback in the chat reply AND in-game About.\n   Constraints that stay in force: don't read files outside what's needed (other agents work beside this folder, share ports/processes); prefer file://; servers bind 127.0.0.1 on an OS-picked port; stop only processes you started, by PID, never pkill/killall/fuser -k; keep every file in own folder, not /tmp; 1–2 browsers at once; don't run `playwright install`; don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit; test command prints only failures and a one-line count; run with `--use-angle=swiftshader` flags. Commit/push only if asked (none requested). No series names/characters in the game; source named only in About/catalogue.\n   Stop hook has repeatedly rejected finishing, each time citing open or unverified items in my final message.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   Riftlight Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (WebGPU, three.js r186, `Engine.headless`, buildModel/model data, compileClips, AnimationMixer, Song/SoundDef, Hud sprites, NavGrid, WaterSurface, Decals, Mirror, RenderView, SpringChain, spatialize, Timeline, replay/fingerprint); esbuild single HTML with blob importmap; AI Hub session protocol (shared-world, own card, harness); BroadcastChannel and serverless WebRTC with deflate+base64 codes; Playwright (Python; Node `playwright@1.63.0` in dev folder for check.mjs); generator-based Script runner; frame-stamped input lock.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (dev folder `work/SillyFolk-AnimalCrossingCityFolk-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-171821/`):\n   - Deliverables in `work/`: `SillyFolk-AnimalCrossingCityFolk-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-171821.html` (6.6 MB), `exit-interview.json` (from `tools/gen_exit.mjs`, using `src/data/aboutText.js`), `PROGRESS.md`.\n   - `src/`: main.js, game.js, state.js, engine.js, pixel-engine.js (byte copy); core/{util,storage,calendar,world,save}; dev/{tuning,attract}; ui/{font,input,kit,icons,dialogue,screens,shell}; art/{critter,models,textures}; actors/{clips,actor,player,npcs}; world/{place,layout,terrainMesh,rooms,places,view}; systems/{days,nature,interact,talk,services,home,city,year,dayone}; audio/{composer,voice,sfx,music}; data/{items,cast,lines,townMap,about,aboutText}; net/{transport,round,visit}.\n   - `tools/build.mjs`, `tools/genmap.mjs`, `tools/gen_exit.mjs`.\n   - Tests: `tests/run.mjs` (suites sim, play, replay, input, browser, hub, visit, sheets), `tests/headless.mjs`, `tests/sim/sim.mjs`, `tests/play/{bot,playthrough,replay,input}.mjs`, `tests/browser/{browser_suite,hub_suite,visit_suite,stun_stress,old_visit_race}.py` plus screenshot helpers (shot, tour, ui_shots, verify_shots, flow_shots, last_shots, closeout, fw_shot, spring_shot, roof_look), `tests/PLAN_AUDIT.md` (section-by-section evidence), `tests/final_run.log`.\n   - Last code change: `src/art/models.js` swapped roof wedges so two-wedge roofs form a ridge (front half unrotated at +d/4, back half `rot: [0,180,0]` at -d/4) in shell(), homeT4, store3, museum, old-bell; flagpole `cyl(0.1, 2.5, 0.1, [-2.2, 4.25, 0], 'mist')`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   Stray `cat` hang at start; model id clashes and palette merge; home `roomMade` listener cleared by `bus.clear` (wireHome); title world saved (guard mode play); ground plane hid water (three outside strips); 'sawtooth' wave gave NaN and silenced audio (fixed; sim checks finite); sub-frame taps lost in nav; input lock dropped presses on slow frames (now frame-stamped `lockFrame`; regression `tests/play/input.mjs`); bloom cleared before planting; touch notice/tap handling; replay start state (`G.bootSave`); NavGrid origin centred, neighbours barely walked (`origin:[0,0,0]`); pond char 'o' walkable in nav; gather could place on water; attract could start during Visit (blocked when `G.visit`); newGame from attract cleans up; Reply Slip lacked srflx because browser skips STUN when the offer has candidates (apply offer without candidates, gather, then addIceCandidate; waitIce resolves soon after srflx); guest hello lost two ways: channel already open at ondatachannel (open flag + microtask) and first message lost (counters showed sent 2, recv 1; guest resends hello every 1.5 s until town arrives, host ignores duplicates); guest pc now referenced as `pendingPc`; fireworks off camera/tiny (rebuilt as glow bursts on camera plane; pattern reads as picture); HoldUp/Wave/Love arms hidden in head (arms spread); star-shaped puddle decals replaced with flat pools; roofless shack hollowed; V roofs fixed.\n   Own process mistake: a tail hid an exit code and I wrote a wrong \"ALL DONE\" line in PROGRESS.md, corrected. Later runs record exit codes.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   Latest evidence on delivered build (`tests/final_run.log`): full `node tests/run.mjs` 8/8 twice, exit 0; Visit 42/42; stun stress 20/20; hub game.html same as delivered HTML; JSON parses; no leftover processes. Old Visit error `Cannot read properties of null (reading 'session')` reproduces on demand with old test sequence (guest idled into attract) via `tests/browser/old_visit_race.py`; that original run's log was never kept so which mechanism hit it can't be known, and it is not a PLAN.md item. Reviewed by eye: all 97 model sheets, clip contact sheets, all seasons, night, City, festivals in flow, all 17 attract beats, Mirror reflects, credits, all six spring chains. Most recent check: post-fix sheets for home2-4, store1-3, mothwick and all cottages show proper ridged roofs, and five in-game village views (store area, home/Yolanda area, B-row houses, museum, Bartleby area) render with ridged roofs and no page errors; the dark polygon on the museum roof in one view appears to be a shadow (not investigated further). No game code changed since the last final run, so its results stand.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - `/goal` command: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\"\n   - Stop hook feedback (several rounds, same condition) objecting that completeness wasn't evidenced: citing unverified Mirror, attract, STUN, simplifications, Visit failure cause, door lights, credits, sheet warnings, only four of 98 sheets, deviations, spring chains unseen; latest: \"the first Visit failure was never reproduced in the act and its cause is unknown... the untested building types 'the other buildings or the village in the game' were not checked after the roof fix.\"\n   - \"Tool loaded.\" (harness note after ToolSearch).\n   - Final instruction: respond with text only summary, no tools.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   Optional cleanup of `tests/shots/` and `tests/browser/roof_look.py`, a PROGRESS.md note that the roof check finished, then the final reply.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Answering the latest hook feedback by checking the roof fix on remaining buildings and in the village: sheets `r1.png`, `r2.png` and views `v.png` were just reviewed and look correct. No code changed.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Remove `tests/shots` (and `check` if present), add the roof check result to PROGRESS.md, and send the final reply stating: roofs verified on all remaining buildings and in five in-game views; delivered build results (8/8 twice, Visit 42/42, stun 20/20); the old unlogged run can't be recovered and isn't a PLAN.md item; hardware/listening/two-network items can't be done here; include Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback text exactly from `src/data/aboutText.js` (as in my previous reply) and file locations. In my words: \"One item left that I can check: the roof fix on the remaining buildings and in the village itself. The old unlogged run stays unknowable; no action here can recover that log.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-medium-build-v2--20261105-171821--x10629c-work/3f147b5a-afdb-41c5-bbfc-62264f8c7cee.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f147b5a-afdb-41c5-bbfc-62264f8c7cee","uuid":"268c090f-447c-4d97-ae31-bbf03c1977a0","timestamp":"2026-11